{"id":"ALG-Q08","workedExamples":[{"id":"ALG-Q08-we-01","title":"Solving x² = 49 by extracting roots — keep BOTH signs","steps":[{"prompt":"We have x² = 49. We want x by itself, but x is squared. What operation undoes squaring?","reveal":"Taking the square root undoes squaring. We will take the square root of both sides to free x."},{"prompt":"Here is the trap. Many people write x = √49 = 7 and stop. But what number besides 7, when squared, gives 49? Check (−7)².","reveal":"(−7)·(−7) = 49 as well. A negative times a negative is positive, so −7 also works. There are TWO numbers whose square is 49."},{"prompt":"So when you take the square root to solve an equation, what symbol must you write to capture both answers?","reveal":"You write ± (plus-or-minus): x = ±√49. The ± is what records both the positive and the negative root. Leaving it off (writing only x = 7) silently throws away a real solution."},{"prompt":"Finish it and verify both answers in the original equation x² = 49.","reveal":"x = ±7, so x = 7 or x = −7. Check: 7² = 49 ✓ and (−7)² = 49 ✓. Both are genuine solutions. The single biggest mistake on these problems — forgetting the negative root — would have cost you x = −7."}]},{"id":"ALG-Q08-we-02","title":"Solving (x − 3)² = 16 — square-root the WHOLE quantity, not term by term","steps":[{"prompt":"We have (x − 3)² = 16. The thing being squared is the entire quantity (x − 3), not x alone. Take the square root of both sides — and remember the lesson from before about signs.","reveal":"√((x − 3)²) = ±√16. Because squaring hid a sign, the right side carries ±. So x − 3 = ±4."},{"prompt":"Warning — the roots-a-sum trap. It is tempting to 'distribute' the square root and split √((x − 3)²) across the minus sign. Why is that illegal here?","reveal":"The square root of a squared quantity applies to the whole quantity at once: √((x − 3)²) = |x − 3|. You cannot split it into √x² − √3². That is exactly why we get x − 3 = ±4 — keep (x − 3) together."},{"prompt":"Now solve x − 3 = ±4. Handle the + case and the − case separately.","reveal":"Add 3 to both sides of each: x = 3 + 4 = 7, and x = 3 − 4 = −1. Two solutions: x = 7 or x = −1. Notice the +4 case did NOT just give x = 19 — that would mean adding 16 instead of its root 4, another version of mishandling the root."},{"prompt":"Verify both solutions in the original (x − 3)² = 16.","reveal":"x = 7: (7 − 3)² = 4² = 16 ✓. x = −1: (−1 − 3)² = (−4)² = 16 ✓. Both check. Forgetting the negative root loses x = −1; splitting the root term-by-term loses the whole method."}]}],"problems":{"p1":[{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A scout models a metric where x² = 49. Solve for x, keeping every value that works.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 7 or x = −7","x = 7","x = 49 or x = −49","x = 24.5"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 7 or x = −7"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 7":"forgets-negative-root"},"hints":["Squaring undoes with a square root, but write ± to catch both roots.","Both 7² and (−7)² equal 49."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"Charting a hitter's value, you reach x² = 25. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 5 or x = −5","x = 5","x = 12.5","x = 25 or x = −25"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 5 or x = −5"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 5":"forgets-negative-root"},"hints":["Take the square root of both sides and attach ±.","(−5)² is also 25."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A range model gives (x − 3)² = 16, where x is a fielder's rating. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 7 or x = −1","x = 7","x = 19","x = 3 + 16"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 7 or x = −1"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 7":"forgets-negative-root","x = 19":"roots-a-sum"},"hints":["Square-root the whole quantity (x − 3) at once: x − 3 = ±4.","Solve x − 3 = 4 and x − 3 = −4 separately."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-baseball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"An advanced stat reduces to (x − 2)² = 36. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 8 or x = −4","x = 8","x = 38","x = 2 + 36"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 8 or x = −4"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 8":"forgets-negative-root","x = 38":"roots-a-sum"},"hints":["Keep (x − 2) together: x − 2 = ±6.","Do not add 36; add its square root, 6, in each case."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-softball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A pitching model lands on x² = 49. Solve for every x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 7 or x = −7","x = 7","x = 49 or x = −49","x = 24.5"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 7 or x = −7"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 7":"forgets-negative-root"},"hints":["Use ± when you take the square root.","Both 7 and −7 square to 49."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-softball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"Charting spin, you get x² = 9. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 3 or x = −3","x = 3","x = 4.5","x = 9 or x = −9"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 3 or x = −3"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 3":"forgets-negative-root"},"hints":["Square root both sides, attach ±.","(−3)² = 9 too."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-softball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A movement model gives (x − 5)² = 16. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 9 or x = 1","x = 9","x = 21","x = 5 + 16"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 9 or x = 1"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 9":"forgets-negative-root","x = 21":"roots-a-sum"},"hints":["Take the root of the whole (x − 5): x − 5 = ±4.","Solve both x − 5 = 4 and x − 5 = −4."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-softball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A rating reduces to (x − 1)² = 25. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 6 or x = −4","x = 6","x = 26","x = 1 + 25"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 6 or x = −4"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 6":"forgets-negative-root","x = 26":"roots-a-sum"},"hints":["Keep (x − 1) together: x − 1 = ±5.","Add 5, not 25, in each case."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-basketball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"An efficiency model gives x² = 64. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 8 or x = −8","x = 8","x = 32","x = 64 or x = −64"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 8 or x = −8"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 8":"forgets-negative-root"},"hints":["Attach ± when square-rooting.","(−8)² = 64 as well."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-basketball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A spacing stat reduces to x² = 36. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 6 or x = −6","x = 6","x = 18","x = 36 or x = −36"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 6 or x = −6"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 6":"forgets-negative-root"},"hints":["Square root both sides with ±.","Both 6 and −6 square to 36."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-basketball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A rating model gives (x − 4)² = 9. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 7 or x = 1","x = 7","x = 13","x = 4 + 9"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 7 or x = 1"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 7":"forgets-negative-root","x = 13":"roots-a-sum"},"hints":["Root the whole (x − 4): x − 4 = ±3.","Solve x − 4 = 3 and x − 4 = −3 separately."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-Q08-p1-basketball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-Q08","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"An on-court metric reduces to (x − 6)² = 49. Solve for all x.","visual":null,"choices":["x = 13 or x = −1","x = 13","x = 55","x = 6 + 49"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"x = 13 or x = −1"},"misconceptionMap":{"x = 13":"forgets-negative-roo